From: ane-stack
Subject: [PATCH 0007] ir: add slice_update for incremental state writes

mil_spec::ir had no slice_update, so an incremental KV-cache append
("write row pos of a state") was inexpressible — the only legal state write
was whole-state. The Block layer already supports write_state; the IR gap
prevented expressing a partial write that ane_lower then stripes per decode
position.

Adds:
- Block::slice_update (vendor/mil_spec/src/lib.rs) emitting a MIL
  slice_update op with begin/end const vectors.
- IR form `su = slice_update(x, begin=[..], end=[..], update=name)` with full
  validation: state must exist, begin/end match rank, ranges are in-bounds,
  and the update's shape equals the region shape (not the whole state).
- Tests: whole-state write, region write, rank mismatch, update-shape
  mismatch, out-of-bounds range rejection.

Stacking: apply after 0001..0006.
